discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** When the worktree path does not exist, every thread's `code.changedSinceComment` silently degrades to `'unknown'` with no stdout warning and no report-level flag. — Failure scenario: `comment-status` is invoked before `fetch-pr` has been run (or after worktree cleanup). `gitOpt` returns `null`, `worktreeStale` is `false`, no warning fires. On a 70-thread PR, all 70 threads show `changedSinceComment: 'unknown'` but the report looks structurally complete — the consumer has no signal that code facts are entirely absent.

Add an explicit guard after `worktreeHeadSha`:

```typescript
if (worktreeHeadSha === null) {
  writeStdoutLine(
    `warning: worktree not found at ${worktree} — code-change facts will be 'unknown' for every thread. Run fetch-pr first.`,
  );
}
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

当 worktree 路径不存在时（如 `fetch-pr` 未运行或 worktree 已清理），每个线程的 `code.changedSinceComment` 静默降级为 `'unknown'`，无 stdout 警告也无报告级标志。消费者看到一份看似完整的报告，却不知道代码事实完全缺失。修复：在 `worktreeHeadSha` 后添加显式警告。

</details>

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

